# --- conversation transcripts: NEVER commit (this tool reads and writes real ones) ---
# Ignored EVERYWHERE, tests included. The suite builds every transcript inside pytest's tmp_path,
# so no committed .jsonl is needed; allowing one under tests/ would only open a place where a
# pasted real transcript could land. Since fleet-guards 2f1edb1 the guard's RUN_SHAPES recognises
# the transcript shapes and blocks a tracked one (see .dataclass.json _armed); this line stays as
# defence in depth, so an untracked transcript never shows up in `git status` to be added.
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz
.fork-*.tmp
exports/

# --- secrets / DB: NEVER commit ---
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
config.json
*.credentials.json
.credentials.json
*credentials*
secrets/
*.token
.env

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/
.venv/

# --- os / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- self-evolve sandbox artefacts ---
.sie/

# --- build/iteration metainfo ---
PROGRESS.md
scratchpad/
*.log
